WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.727
Overall summaries can hide differences between groups.

00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:12.397
For example, the overall average order amount may look reasonable, but one region may have much higher values than the

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:20.540
others. Grouped EDA helps us compare categories such as regions, departments, channels, or customer segments.

00:00:21.071 --> 00:00:25.138
Run the code and compare count, median, mean, and maximum for each region.

00:00:25.138 --> 00:00:33.868
The count matters because a group with only one or two observations should be interpreted cautiously.

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:38.488
Also notice the difference between mean and median within each group.

00:00:38.488 --> 00:00:44.198
If one group has an extreme value, the mean may move much more than the median.

00:00:44.198 --> 00:00:49.238
At this stage, treat group differences as patterns to investigate.

00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:55.943
A difference in a summary table does not automatically mean the groups are statistically different in the larger

00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:56.806
population.
